<title>ITALY: IMI cons net profit jumps in H1.</title>
<headline>IMI cons net profit jumps in H1.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Consolidated net profit	341.5 vs   210.3</p>
<p>    Parent net profit		238.8 vs   219.9</p>
<p>    Parent operating margin	501.3 vs   473.9</p>
<p>    Parent interest margin	 448.7 vs   422.9</p>
<p>    Parent intermediary margin   683.5 vs   680.5</p>
<p>Note: Full name Istituto Mobiliare Italiano.  </p>
<p>    Parent client loans	   43,564.8 vs 43,414.2</p>
<p>    Parent client deposits	 2,255.4 vs  2,625.4</p>
<p>    Parent bond deposits	  20,435.2 vs 20,439.4</p>
<p>    Parent reserves		  1,583.0 vs  1,560.0</p>
<p>Note: IMI said in a statement it expected total loans in 1996 to roughly equal total loans in 1995.</p>
<p>It said it expected consolidated 1996 net profits to be stronger than 1995's 552 billion lire, although not as big in percentage terms as the 62.4 percent jump in group net profits recorded in the first half of the year. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
